<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>DRT.FM Competitor Checks — Hands-On Review</title>
<style>
*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
body{font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;background:#0d0d12;color:#e0e0e8;line-height:1.6;padding-top:56px}

/* NAV */
nav{position:fixed;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:100;background:#0a0a10;border-bottom:1px solid #1e1e2e;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;padding:0 16px;height:56px;overflow-x:auto}
nav::-webkit-scrollbar{height:3px}nav::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:#2a2a3e}
.nav-label{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#3a3a5a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;white-space:nowrap;margin-right:8px;padding-right:12px;border-right:1px solid #1e1e2e}
.tab-btn{flex-shrink:0;padding:6px 16px;border-radius:6px;border:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;background:transparent;transition:all .15s;white-space:nowrap}
.tab-btn:hover{background:#1e1e2e}
.tab-btn.active{color:#fff}
.tab-summary{color:#34d399}.tab-summary.active{background:#0a2820}
.tab-kindroid{color:#5eead4}.tab-kindroid.active{background:#0a2820}
.tab-lovescape{color:#f0abfc}.tab-lovescape.active{background:#260a30}
.tab-swipey{color:#fb7185}.tab-swipey.active{background:#2a0a14}
.tab-sweetdream{color:#a78bfa}.tab-sweetdream.active{background:#16102a}
.tab-nomi{color:#22d3ee}.tab-nomi.active{background:#0a2228}
.tab-candy{color:#ff4da6}.tab-candy.active{background:#280818}
.tab-od{color:#4da6ff}.tab-od.active{background:#0a1828}
.tab-sd{color:#9b4dca}.tab-sd.active{background:#1e0a2e}
.tab-ggpt{color:#ff6b9d}.tab-ggpt.active{background:#2a1020}
.tab-pc{color:#ff9f43}.tab-pc.active{background:#1e1200}
.tab-joi{color:#f9ca24}.tab-joi.active{background:#1e1800}
.private-badge{margin-left:auto;flex-shrink:0;background:#3a1020;border:1px solid #6a2040;color:#ff8aaa;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;padding:3px 10px;border-radius:20px}

/* SECTIONS */
.section{display:none;max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:32px 32px 80px}
.section.active{display:block}

/* HERO */
.hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#061a0a,#0a2a10);border:1px solid #1a4a1a;border-radius:14px;padding:26px 32px;margin-bottom:32px}
.hero h1{font-size:22px;font-weight:800;color:#34d399;margin-bottom:8px}
.hero p{font-size:14px;color:#7ed4b8;max-width:760px;line-height:1.6}
.hero .meta{margin-top:14px;font-size:12px;color:#4a8a4a}

/* COMPETITOR HEADER */
.check-header{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#0e0e16,#13131c);border:1px solid #2a2a3e;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px;margin-bottom:24px}
.check-header h1{font-size:28px;font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin-bottom:6px}
.check-header .meta{font-size:13px;color:#7070a0;font-family:'SF Mono','Monaco',monospace}
.check-header .priority{margin-top:12px;font-size:13px;color:#a8d4b8;background:#0a1a14;border:1px solid #1a3a28;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;line-height:1.5}

/* SECTION HEADERS (within a tab) */
h2.zone{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#5eead4;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1.5px;margin:32px 0 14px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:2px solid #1e1e2e;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px}
h2.zone .zone-badge{font-size:10px;background:#0a2820;color:#5eead4;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:4px;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px}

/* QUICK REFERENCE */
.quick-ref{background:#0e0e16;border:1px solid #2a2a3e;border-radius:12px;padding:20px 24px}
.quick-ref-group{margin-bottom:18px}
.quick-ref-group:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.quick-ref-group-title{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#a78bfa;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px}
.quick-ref ul{list-style:none}
.quick-ref li{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:flex-start;padding:6px 0;font-size:13px;color:#c0c0d8;line-height:1.6}
.quick-ref li input[type="checkbox"]{margin-top:5px;flex-shrink:0;accent-color:#5eead4}
.quick-ref li strong{color:#fff;font-weight:600}
.quick-ref li em{color:#7070a0;font-style:italic;font-size:12px;display:block;margin-top:2px}
.ambient{margin-top:18px;padding:12px 14px;background:#0a1828;border:1px solid #1a3a5e;border-radius:8px;font-size:12px;color:#a8c8e8;line-height:1.5}
.ambient strong{color:#60a5fa}

/* FINDINGS */
.findings{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
.finding{background:#0e0e16;border:1px solid #2a2a3e;border-radius:10px;padding:14px 18px}
.finding-meta{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#7070a0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.8px;margin-bottom:6px;display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}
.finding-meta .time{color:#5060a0}
.tag{background:#1e1e2e;color:#a78bfa;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:3px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.5px}
.tag-standout{background:#2a1a4e;color:#c08aff}
.tag-ick{background:#2a0a14;color:#ff8aaa}
.tag-speed{background:#1e1200;color:#ff9f43}
.finding-body{font-size:14px;color:#d0d0e8;line-height:1.6}
.finding-body strong{color:#fff}
.findings-empty{padding:40px 20px;text-align:center;color:#5060a0;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;background:#0a0a12;border:1px dashed #2a2a3e;border-radius:10px}
.check-shot{display:block;max-width:100%;width:auto;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid #2a2a3e;margin:10px 0}

/* ACTIONS / STANDOUT */
.actions{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#16103a,#0e0a20);border:1px solid #3a2a6e;border-radius:14px;padding:24px 28px}
.actions-empty{color:#7070a0;font-style:italic;font-size:13px}
.verdict{font-size:14px;color:#d0c8e8;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:18px;padding-bottom:16px;border-bottom:1px solid #2a2050}
.action-group{margin-bottom:18px}
.action-group:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.action-group-title{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px;margin-bottom:8px}
.steal .action-group-title{color:#4ade80}
.win .action-group-title{color:#60a5fa}
.avoid .action-group-title{color:#ff6b6b}
.action-group ul{list-style:none}
.action-group li{font-size:13px;color:#b0b0c8;padding:5px 0;padding-left:18px;position:relative;line-height:1.6}
.action-group li::before{position:absolute;left:0;top:5px;font-weight:700}
.steal li::before{content:'+';color:#4ade80}
.win li::before{content:'✓';color:#60a5fa}
.avoid li::before{content:'!';color:#ff6b6b}
.scores{margin-top:16px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid #2a2050;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(140px,1fr));gap:10px}
.score{background:#0a0814;border:1px solid #2a2050;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 12px;text-align:center}
.score-label{font-size:10px;color:#7070a0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px}
.score-value{font-size:22px;font-weight:800;color:#c08aff;line-height:1.2;margin-top:2px}

/* SUMMARY TAB */
.always-on{background:#0e0e16;border:1px solid #2a2a3e;border-radius:12px;padding:22px 26px;margin-bottom:24px}
.always-on h3{font-size:14px;color:#5eead4;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:14px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:1px}
.always-on ol{padding-left:22px;color:#c0c0d8;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8}
.always-on ol li{margin-bottom:6px}
.always-on ol li strong{color:#fff}

.workflow-card{background:#0a1a14;border:1px solid #1a4838;border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:13px;color:#a8d4b8;line-height:1.7}
.workflow-card code{background:#0a2820;color:#5eead4;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-family:'SF Mono','Monaco',monospace;font-size:12px}
.workflow-card strong{color:#34d399}

.status-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(180px,1fr));gap:10px;margin-top:14px}
.status-card{background:#0e0e16;border:1px solid #2a2a3e;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px}
.status-card-name{font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:#e0e0e8;margin-bottom:4px}
.status-card-state{font-size:11px;color:#7070a0;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.5px}
.status-done{border-color:#1a4a1a;background:#0a1a0a}
.status-done .status-card-state{color:#4ade80}
.status-progress{border-color:#1e3a5e;background:#0a1828}
.status-progress .status-card-state{color:#60a5fa}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <span class="nav-label">Competitor Checks</span>
  <button class="tab-btn tab-summary active" onclick="show('summary',this)">📋 Summary</button>
  <button class="tab-btn tab-kindroid" onclick="show('kindroid',this)">Kindroid</button>
  <button class="tab-btn tab-ggpt" onclick="show('girlfriendgpt',this)">GirlfriendGPT</button>
  <span class="private-badge">DRT.FM · Private</span>
</nav>

<!-- ==================== SUMMARY ==================== -->
<div id="summary" class="section active">

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Hands-On Competitor Review</h1>
  <p>One tab per competitor. Quick Reference Checklist at top of each tab, Findings (chronological, tagged, with screenshots) in the middle, Standout &amp; Actions for Steve at the bottom. Each competitor can be reviewed in a fresh Claude tab — just type <code style="background:#0a2820;color:#5eead4;padding:1px 6px;border-radius:4px;font-family:'SF Mono',monospace;font-size:12px">/competitor-checks &lt;site&gt;</code> to load the workflow.</p>
  <div class="meta">First session: Kindroid · Started 2026-05-17</div>
</div>

<div class="workflow-card">
  <strong>How this works:</strong><br>
  1. Dainis opens a paid account on a competitor site.<br>
  2. Browses freely. Shares notes + screenshots in chat (screenshots auto-save to <code>~/Downloads/SCR-*.png|jpeg</code>).<br>
  3. Claude catalogues notes into the right tab, moves screenshots into <code>assets/checks/&lt;slug&gt;/</code>, and prompts for Chrome DevTools deep-dives when a feature looks standout.<br>
  4. At session end, Claude generates the <strong>Standout &amp; Actions for Steve</strong> zone — verdict, steal-list, win-list, avoid-list, 1-10 scores.<br>
  5. Then recommends the next competitor.
</div>

<h2 class="zone">Always-On Checklist <span class="zone-badge">Every competitor</span></h2>
<div class="always-on">
  <h3>The 6 items applied to every site</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Time it (seconds):</strong> first chat response · first image · first video · first voice word · clicks from homepage → first message.</li>
    <li><strong>Screenshots to always grab:</strong> chat input area · subscription/upgrade page · homepage (logged in) · mobile view.</li>
    <li><strong>Ick Test — flag any:</strong> AI breaking character · unexpected NSFW blocks · mid-chat upsell prompts · UI bugs · moments that felt genuinely "human."</li>
    <li><strong>Score 1-10 at end:</strong> memory · voice emotional quality · image face consistency · NSFW consistency · overall "companion vs chatbot" feel.</li>
    <li><strong>Steal:</strong> one thing to copy into DRT.FM immediately.</li>
    <li><strong>Win:</strong> one thing DRT.FM already does better.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

<h2 class="zone">Progress <span class="zone-badge">11 sites in scope</span></h2>
<div class="status-grid">
  <div class="status-card status-done"><div class="status-card-name">Kindroid</div><div class="status-card-state">Done · 2026-05-17</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">LoveScape</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">Swipey</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">SweetDream</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">Nomi</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">Candy.AI</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">OurDream</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">SecretDesires</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card status-progress"><div class="status-card-name">GirlfriendGPT</div><div class="status-card-state">In progress · 2026-05-17</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">Promptchan</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
  <div class="status-card"><div class="status-card-name">Joi.AI</div><div class="status-card-state">Pending</div></div>
</div>

</div>

<!-- ==================== KINDROID ==================== -->
<div id="kindroid" class="section">

<div class="check-header">
  <h1>Kindroid</h1>
  <div class="meta">kindroid.ai · tier picked: ___ · session date: 2026-05-17</div>
  <div class="priority"><strong>Why this site:</strong> First major platform shipping live AI video calls (Mar 2026), Cascaded Memory (5-layer), user-editable Codex backstory, Shared Kindroid remix marketplace, screen sharing in calls, group video, multi-language mid-chat. 5-person team shipping aggressively. 1.2M downloads. Per-credit billing is unusual — worth understanding the unit economics.</div>
</div>

<h2 class="zone">Standout &amp; Actions for Steve <span class="zone-badge">Session complete · 2026-05-17</span></h2>
<div class="findings">

  <div class="finding" data-tags="signup,billing">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session start · signup · billing</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Payment processor: Chargebee.</strong> 3-day free trial gated behind phone number SMS verification — verified, worked. Smart anti-abuse: without phone verification you must pay immediately, so bulk trial farming is blocked. Cheapest paid tier: <strong>$13.99/mo</strong> (after 3-day trial).
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/01-subscription-page.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="signup,ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session start · signup · ux · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Post-signup welcome notification:</strong> 🎉 Welcome to Kindroid Premium! 🎉 — congratulatory message with first-best-steps guidance so the user is not lost. Clean onboarding hook. <em>Standout: immediate orientation after payment, not just a blank dashboard.</em>
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/02-welcome-onboarding-notification.jpeg" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="ux">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session start · ux</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>First main dashboard.</strong>
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/03-main-dashboard.jpeg" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>


  <div class="finding" data-tags="chat,ux">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · chat · ux</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Chat break — clear recent context.</strong> "Chat break" button in settings wipes recent conversation context for a fresh start without deleting the relationship/memory entirely. Useful for resetting a conversation that went off-rails without losing the character.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/40-chat-break.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="voice,chat,ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · voice · chat · ux · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Voice call appears inline in chat thread.</strong> After a call, a record of it shows up in the chat where it happened. The call and the text conversation are in the same timeline. This partially addresses the earlier "siloed" finding — the call does leave a trace in chat. The seam going <em>into</em> the call is still clunky (separate top-level button) but the <em>return</em> to chat is smooth.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/41-voice-call-in-chat.png" class="check-shot">
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/42-voice-call-in-chat-2.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="voice,billing,ux">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · voice · billing · ux</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Voice selection — 5 defaults + custom voice creation, tied to slot count.</strong><br><br>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>Default voices:</strong> 5 (Default Voice 1–5, generic names — no personality)</li>
        <li><strong>Custom Voices:</strong> 0/20 available — "You can have as many custom voice slots as you do Kindroid slots." Custom voices scale with character slot purchases.</li>
        <li><strong>Voice Model V3 costs 15× V2.</strong> V2 is "experimental and subject to change." V3 is production-stable but burns credits ~15× faster per call minute. This explains why fast-voice ON still felt affordable — most users are probably on V2 without knowing it.</li>
      </ul>
      The 5 default voices have no names or personality descriptors — just numbered. Low effort for such a central feature; DRT.FM can easily beat this with named, characterised voice presets.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/45-voice-selection.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="billing,ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · billing · ux · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Purchase Kindroid &amp; Groupchat Slots — add-on pricing on top of subscription.</strong> Separate from the monthly subscription, users buy character + group slot packs:<br><br>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>1 Kindroid + 2 Group Slots:</strong> $2.99</li>
        <li><strong>4 Kindroid + 8 Group Slots:</strong> $9.99 (Best value)</li>
      </ul>
      "Each Kindroid slot also gives you 2 group chat/scenario slots." So group calls are gated behind buying extra character slots — elegant bundling. Base subscription likely includes 1 Kindroid. Additional characters are $2.99 each (or $2.50 in the 4-pack). Custom voice slots scale with Kindroid slots.<br><br>
      This is a smart upsell: users who want more characters pay incrementally, and each purchase also unlocks group chat — two features for one purchase decision.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/46-purchase-group-slots.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="memory,ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · memory · ux · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Character memory architecture — 5 distinct input layers, all user-controllable.</strong> The character settings page exposes every memory layer with influence ratings:<br><br>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>Backstory</strong> — 407/2500 chars. "Strong influence." 3rd-person narrative about the character.</li>
        <li><strong>Response directive</strong> — 96/250 chars. <strong>"Very strong influence."</strong> Controls length, tone, personality, formatting. Most powerful lever.</li>
        <li><strong>Key memories</strong> — 0/1000 chars. "Moderate influence." Things the AI should always remember.</li>
        <li><strong>Example message</strong> — 0/750 chars. "Moderate influence." Reference for tone, mannerisms, message length — written from the character's perspective.</li>
        <li><strong>Journal entries</strong> — keyphrase-triggered recall. Athena's Journal (character-specific) + Global Journal (shared across all Kindroids). AI recalls entries when you mention a matching keyphrase. Flexible knowledge base / lore system.</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/47-character-memory-layers.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · ux · settings · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Account-wide + Kindroid-specific settings — far more depth than the UI suggests.</strong> Full inventory of notable settings found:<br><br>
      <strong>Account-wide:</strong>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>User personas</strong> — multiple personas, auto-switch when chatting with a tied Kindroid</li>
        <li><strong>Text messaging</strong> — text your Kindroid from your phone's messaging app (iMessage/SMS integration)</li>
        <li><strong>Calendar integration</strong> — connectable (not set up)</li>
        <li><strong>Repetition guard</strong> — ON by default, auto-retries to prevent repetitive responses</li>
        <li><strong>Beta testing</strong> — password-gated beta features</li>
      </ul>
      <strong>Kindroid-specific:</strong>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>Tied user persona</strong> — auto-switches your persona when you open this character's chat</li>
        <li><strong>Proactivity controls</strong> — configure live chat actions, away actions, inactivity actions independently</li>
        <li><strong>Time awareness</strong> — ON: AI knows time of day, timing between messages (Rhapsody+ models only)</li>
        <li><strong>Chat dynamism: 0.95</strong> — slider controlling how stable vs. dynamic the AI is in conversation and calls</li>
        <li><strong>Long term memory controls</strong> — toggle whether this Kindroid consolidates to long-term memory</li>
        <li><strong>Chat background</strong> — set selfies or uploaded images as chat backgrounds</li>
        <li><strong>API &amp; advanced integrations</strong> — developer API access</li>
      </ul>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/48-settings-menu.png" class="check-shot">
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/49-account-wide-settings.png" class="check-shot">
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/50-kindroid-specific-settings.png" class="check-shot">
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/51-kindroid-specific-settings-2.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · ux · overall verdict</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>UX overall verdict: "deceptively deep."</strong> First impression is clunky and sparse. But the more you use it, the more you find: top nav has the key daily-use features (chat, selfies, call, gifts), sidebar hides deep functionality, in-chat settings are extensive, call settings are extensive. The product is built for power users who explore — not for casual onboarding.<br><br>
      <em>Ick:</em> discoverability is poor. Many of the best features (journal recall, dynamism slider, response directive, proactivity controls) are invisible until you go looking. Most users never find them.<br><br>
      <em>Opportunity for DRT.FM:</em> same depth, better surfacing. Progressive disclosure — show simple defaults, reveal power tools as users engage more.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="image,ux,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · image · ux · tech · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Selfies model picker — 6 internal model versions, all custom-named.</strong> Kindroid has built and versioned their own image generation pipeline:<br><br>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>Canon (V4)</strong> — oldest</li>
        <li><strong>Odyssey (V5)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Palette (V6)</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Tableau</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Atelier</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Latest (Atelier)</strong> ✓ default — always maps to newest</li>
      </ul>
      No external provider named — deliberate branding. Likely fine-tuned versions of Stable Diffusion / SDXL / FLUX, self-hosted on GCP. The naming convention (art-world terms: Tableau, Atelier, Palette) is a nice product touch.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/43-video-models.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="video,tech">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · video · tech</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Video model picker — V3 (Latest), internal versioning.</strong> "Always uses the newest video model. Currently maps to V3." V1 → V2 → V3 progression = they own and iterate the face-animation pipeline themselves. Combined with server-side processing through LiveKit, this is almost certainly a fine-tuned open-source face animation model (SadTalker / Wav2Lip derivative) self-hosted on GCP — not a per-call external API. A 5-person team paying HeyGen/D-ID per minute at their scale would be prohibitively expensive.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/44-video-models-2.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="tech">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · tech · infra</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Backend stack confirmed from get-call-token headers.</strong>
      <ul style="margin:6px 0 6px 16px;line-height:1.9">
        <li><strong>Cloud:</strong> GCP (server: Google Frontend)</li>
        <li><strong>Runtime:</strong> Node.js / Express (x-powered-by: Express)</li>
        <li><strong>Auth:</strong> Firebase JWT (Google auth) passed as Bearer token</li>
        <li><strong>Call token:</strong> POST 95-byte payload → 1112-byte response = LiveKit JWT with room config</li>
        <li><strong>CDN:</strong> Cloudflare for assets</li>
      </ul>
      Full confirmed stack: <strong>Next.js → GCP/Express API → Firebase auth + Firestore → LiveKit WebRTC → self-hosted face animation models → Chargebee billing → Sentry monitoring → GA4 analytics.</strong>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finding" data-tags="voice,speed,standout">
    <div class="finding-meta">Session · voice · speed · tech · standout</div>
    <div class="finding-body">
      <strong>Call infra: LiveKit Cloud + Firebase Firestore.</strong> Network tab during active call shows:<br><br>
      <code>https://kindroid-hi9mxshg.livekit.cloud/settings/regions</code> — LiveKit Cloud is their WebRTC transport layer (real-time audio/video streaming). LiveKit is open-source WebRTC infra, widely used for low-latency voice/video. The <code>/settings/regions</code> call is automatic region selection for lowest-latency routing.<br><br>
      <strong>Why the voice model is invisible in DevTools:</strong> The TTS synthesis (whatever model powers the voice) is called <em>server-side</em> on Kindroid's backend, then streamed back to the client as audio via LiveKit. It won't show up as a client-side API call — it's behind their server. To confirm the provider we'd need server-side access or a leak in response headers.<br><br>
      <strong>Latency verdict:</strong> LiveKit + server-side TTS streaming = fast. This is the right architecture for low-latency voice. Firestore handles real-time state sync (chat history, call state) alongside the call.
      <br><br>
      <img src="assets/checks/kindroid/25-devtools-livekit-call-infra.png" class="check-shot">
    </div>
  </div>

