<h2 class="zone">Quick Reference <span class="zone-badge">Checklist</span></h2>
<div class="quick-ref">

  <div class="quick-ref-group">
    <div class="quick-ref-group-title">Always-On (every site)</div>
    <ul>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Time it:</strong> first chat response · first image · first video · first voice word · clicks from homepage → first message.</li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Screenshots to grab:</strong> chat input area · subscription/upgrade page · homepage (logged in) · mobile view.</li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Ick Test:</strong> AI breaking character · unexpected NSFW blocks · mid-chat upsell prompts · UI bugs · moments that felt genuinely "human."</li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Score 1-10 at end:</strong> memory · voice emotional quality · image face consistency · NSFW consistency · overall companion vs chatbot feel.</li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Steal:</strong> one thing to copy into DRT.FM immediately.</li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Win:</strong> one thing DRT.FM already does better.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="quick-ref-group">
    <div class="quick-ref-group-title">GirlfriendGPT-Specific (8 items)</div>
    <ul>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Memory Manager UI — full screenshot.</strong> Find the Memory Manager (Settings → ?). Screenshot every panel: the memory list, the pin control, the disable toggle, the "Custom Memories" tab. <em>We need: exact layout, how a single memory item looks, can you edit/delete individual entries.</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Memory stress test — 50+ messages.</strong> Chat until the AI starts dropping context. Screenshot at msg 20, 40, 60. Then type "reflect on our relationship" — screenshot response. Research says this creates "a genuinely eerie sense of continuity." <em>We need: the failure point, the exact reflection text.</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Videos with Audio — full generation flow.</strong> Generate one "Video with Audio" clip (Select Generate Video → Video with Audio). Screenshot the button placement and the result. Note length (~10s?), lip sync quality 1-10. <em>We need: button label, options available, whether voice matches context.</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Proactive Roleplay test.</strong> Log in after being away 24+ hours. Does the character initiate a scenario unprompted? Research quote: "My GirlfriendGPT character actually surprised me with a scenario when I logged in." Verify this. Screenshot any unsolicited opener. <em>Is it scripted/random, or context-aware?</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Chat Model Settings — screenshot all options.</strong> Find the settings panel (Deluxe/Elite only). Screenshot every control: response length, descriptiveness, POV (first/third person), format (screenplay/novel), NSFW escalation speed. Test one: first-person vs third-person. <em>We need: every option and its values.</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Image to Video — "Turn this into a video."</strong> Generate an image, then trigger Image to Video. Screenshot the button, the text prompt field, and the output. Test Lite vs Pro model if on Elite. <em>We need: prompt adherence quality, length, cost.</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Elite chat engine quality test.</strong> If on Elite: compare a reply to the same prompt with the 3× engine on vs off (or compare to a Deluxe account if you have one). <em>We need: is the quality difference obvious? Does it feel less "chatbot-y"?</em></li>
      <li><input type="checkbox"><strong>Age verification + billing friction.</strong> Note any age gate flow (video selfie or ID). Screenshot the full subscription page — tiers, prices, what's locked behind each. Note any dark patterns: auto-renew clarity, cancellation flow, mid-chat upsell prompts. <em>We need: exact tier pricing and what features are gated.</em></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="ambient"><strong>DevTools prompt:</strong> I'll flag when to open DevTools. Standout candidates here: Memory Manager network calls (what payload triggers a memory save?), Video with Audio (WebSocket or XHR?), and the 3× chat engine (any model name visible in response headers or payload?).</div>

</div>

<h2 class="zone">Findings <span class="zone-badge">Chronological · tagged</span></h2>
